    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s alliance turned the Electorate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> into a kingdom in 1806, the second largest German state.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximilian-von-montgelas">Montgelas</a> built a centralised, tolerant administration, and the constitution of 1818 created one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s first parliaments.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludwig-i-of-bavaria">Ludwig I</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludwig-ii-of-bavaria">Ludwig II</a> made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavarian-alps">Bavarian Alps</a> famous for art, architecture and fantasy castles.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oktoberfest">Oktoberfest</a> began in October 1810 as a public celebration of the wedding of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludwig-i-of-bavaria">Crown Prince Ludwig</a>, the future Ludwig I, to Princess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/therese-of-saxe-hildburghausen">Therese of Saxe-Hildburghausen</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

